WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:04.950
What happens when a visitor takes the place of an acting teacher?

2
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:09.950
Observer, director and performer.
Moving between these positions is the core of the experience.

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.750
The visitor chooses one of fourteen bilingual theme cards
… or types a premise of their own.
Choose a story title you like

4
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.750
A language model generates the given circumstances
and each character’s objective.
Press “Let them begin” to start the scene

5
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:24.250
A and B improvise in turn, one large line at a time.
It produces every line live; nothing is pre-scripted.
Watch: the scene runs on its own

6
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:28.650
After every four AI lines the scene pauses so the visitor
can decide whether to keep watching or intervene.
Click Direct to give a new action

7
00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:33.850
Like an acting teacher, the visitor gives a new action to A, B or both.
A role-specific direction is sent only to that character.
Pick A, B or Both, then give the direction

8
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:39.850
The other must respond to what it actually hears. A direction is not a command:
the character may follow it, resist it or misread it.
Keep watching, or step in again

9
00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:43.450
Take a role.
Click Take a role to play A or B

10
00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:49.950
The visitor replaces A or B and types that character’s lines, while the AI partner keeps improvising.
The role can be handed back at any time, and the AI resumes it from the human’s choices.

11
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:56.350
The visitor names a new character and a reason to be there,
and a third chair lights up.
Click Join, name your character, then Enter as C

12
00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:02.150
C is always human; the system never writes C’s lines.
Type C’s line; A and B respond

13
00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:07.750
The two AI characters must now deal with a human
who has changed the stakes for both of them.

14
00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:12.250
Visitors may export a record of their scene that distinguishes human from AI lines.

15
00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:20.250
It translates rehearsal-room techniques into a reusable interaction model for human–AI collaboration,
in which the human may direct, substitute or co-perform within the same continuous scene.

